e to be. Tracing the complex genealogy of Tantra as a category within the history of religions, Hugh B. Urban reveals how it has been formed through the interplay of popular and scholarly imaginations. Tantra emerges as a product of mirroring and misrepresentation at work between East and West--a dialectical category born out of the ongoing play between Western and Indian minds. Combining historical detail, textual analysis, popular cultural phenomena, and critical theory, this book shows Tantra as a shifting amalgam of fantasies, fears, and wish-fulfillment, at once native and Other, that strikes at the very heart of our constructions of the exotic Orient and the contemporary West\"--Publisher's description."},"latest_revision":15,"revision":15,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-09-13T17:11:48.343035"}}},"ISBN:9788120829329":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9788120829329","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL9888114M/Tantra","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL9888114M/Tantra","details":{"identifiers":{"goodreads":["6839587"],"librarything":["687556"]},"title":"Tantra","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL1479861A","name":"Hugh B. Urban"}],"publish_date":"May 30, 2005","publishers":["Motilal Banarsidass,India"],"isbn_13":["9788120829329"],"physical_format":"Paperback","isbn_10":["8120829328"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["History of religion"],"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The category \"Tantra\" is a basic and familiar one today in the vocabulary of most scholars of religious and generally considered one of the most important and controversial forms of Asian religion."},"source_records":["amazon:8120829328"],"key":"/books/OL9888114M","number_of_pages":388,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL5962859W"}],"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T09:38:13.731961"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/dat